# LRU Cache
least recently used Cache

GET and PUT operations should be supported.
We will use the hashmap to track the key value. 

# Funtionality of GET:
The values of the DLL will be added to the hashmap (index, refernece to the value)
Everytime we get a value, it should be added to the head to note that the node was recently used. pushing back all other nodes towards the tail.


# Fuunctionaility of PUT:
Case 1: Value already exists
1. Check is the value already exits in the DLL. If yes then update the value in the dll as well as the hashmap refernece to the value
2. Then again, add this node to the start to mark as recently used, poushing all other towards the tail.

Case 2: Value does not exits
1. check capacity, less adequent, then add to add the new node and also update the hashmap
2. If not adequent capacity then remove the least recently used value from the cache dll tail
3. then add the node to the head and also update the hashmap


# Summarize:
# GET:
Fetch value from HashMap
move the node to head

# PUT:
case1: old entry updated
update the node value in dll
move the node to head
update the value refernece in the hashmap

case2: New entry
case a: capacity adequent:
1. add the new noe to the head
2. add the referenece to the value in the hashMap

caseb: no adequent capacity
1. remove one node from the tai - least recently used
2. add the new node to the head
3. add the refernence to the value in the hashmap